# two-design — licence scope

This repository contains separately licensed material. It is not all covered
by a single licence. The grants below apply only to first-party material and
only to rights the contributors have authority to license. Existing
third-party copyright and licence notices remain in force.

## First-party code and design tokens — MIT

First-party code, configuration and design tokens are licensed under the MIT
License in LICENSES/MIT.txt. This includes tokens/, tools/, ci/, .github/,
.githooks/, package.json, preview/ HTML and CSS (including generated CSS), and
code examples in the documentation.

This grant does not include the reserved brand marks or third-party assets
listed below, even when code or a preview references or displays them.

## First-party documentation — CC-BY-4.0

First-party documentation prose in README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md and docs/ is
licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International Public
License (CC-BY-4.0), reproduced in LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Attribute the documentation to the TogetherWeOwn contributors, retain supplied
notices, link to the source (https://github.com/TogetherWeOwn/two-design) and
licence, and indicate changes as required by that licence. This is a summary;
the full licence text governs. Code examples are MIT as specified above.
Brand marks and third-party material appearing in documentation are excluded
from this documentation grant.

## Brand marks — all rights reserved

The TWO / Together We Own names, logos and brand-mark artwork are reserved;
no trademark licence or permission to reuse that artwork is granted by the
MIT or CC-BY-4.0 licences. This includes:

- assets/brand/two-icon-256.png
- assets/brand/two-splash-1024.png

See assets/brand/NOTICE.md. Displaying a mark in documentation or a preview,
or supplying installation instructions, does not put it under either open
licence. Statutory exceptions and any separately granted permissions are
unaffected. The reusable code and tokens do not require permission to use
under their MIT licence; the reservation applies to the marks, not the
colour values, spacing or other design tokens.

## Third-party material — original licences retained

The Archivo fonts are third-party material, not claimed as TogetherWeOwn's
work. assets/fonts/archivo-latin.woff2 and
assets/fonts/archivo-latin-ext.woff2 remain licensed under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1. The original copyright notice and full licence are preserved in
assets/fonts/Archivo-OFL.txt and must accompany redistributed font copies in
accordance with that licence. Neither MIT nor CC-BY-4.0 replaces the OFL.

Other third-party material, if added, retains its own notices and terms; none
of the first-party grants above purports to relicense it. Licence texts are
reproduced notices, not claimed as first-party documentation.

## Publication is separate

These licence boundaries do not change repository visibility or publish a
package. package.json remains private: true. Making a GitHub repository
public would not publish an npm package or grant rights to its reserved brand
marks; package publication is a separate operation.
